# Arena Set Cracker (frontend)

## Product

Offline-first Angular app for **cracking** one installed **Magic: The Gathering Arena** set at a time: WotC sells an assignment puzzle; every card in the set belongs in some deck, even when that is not printed on the box. The user assigns the catalog. The app supplies slices, not a verdict.

Happy path today: install a set (Scryfall) → open it → paste an Arena export → persist locally → reload and still see the list.

**Invariant:** decks and Arena imports resolve only against the focused set’s catalog. Lines that do not match that catalog are stripped; notify the user. Do not design for multi-set decklists.

Color identity is not capped at two; do not bake guild/dual as the only shape of a deck.

**Client** owns discovery tooling against the local catalog: oracle-text analysis and, later, real NLP. User-supplied source text (the work WotC adapted—e.g. a chapter the user provides, not a bundled book) is a valid slice against the focused set. Do not hide the catalog behind an emergence score.

**Backend** is for community-aggregated insight (e.g. pairing rates: “60% of players put this card with a card already in your deck”), not for streaming Scryfall or running the user’s discovery job.

## Stack map

- Angular 22 standalone + Material
- Local vault: Drizzle schema (`public/drizzle/0000_*.sql` bootstrap). Empty vault applies that SQL; existing DB loads as-is. No startup ALTER / column-ensure. No in-place upgrades until a client is shipped; layout change means wipe `mtg_vault.db` (and the browser IndexedDB key).
- Persist hosts via `VAULT_ENGINE_TOKEN`: browser = sql.js + IndexedDB (`BrowserVaultEngine`); Electron = `better-sqlite3` in main (`ElectronVaultEngine`); Capacitor = `@capacitor-community/sqlite` (`CapacitorVaultEngine`).
- Domain I/O: `VaultStore` (local CRUD + enqueue syncable sets/decks). Drain: `SyncService` → NDJSON bulk-sync. Same-DB `sync_queue` outbox.
- Also: Capacitor mobile, optional cloud API via `src/assets/config.json` (`baseUrl`)

## Where the brain lives

| Concern | Owner |
|---------|--------|
| Installed sets + active workspace (set, cards, decks) | `SetService` |
| Active deck scratchpad + flush/persist | `DeckService` |
| Arena parse + name resolve within catalog | `shared/models/deck/deck.utils.ts` |
| Remaining pool + pattern concentration | `remaining-pool.ts`, `concentration.ts` (+ `concentration.worker.ts`) |
| Set board theme-phrase drag | `SetBoardDrag` |
| Shared drag primitives | `shared/drag/drag.utils.ts` |
| Deck builder card drag zones | `DeckBuilderDrag` |
| SQLite schema (create only) | `core/sqlite/sqlite.schema.ts`, `public/drizzle/` (`0000` bootstrap) |
| Local vault CRUD + sync enqueue | `VaultStore` |
| Outbox drain → server | `SyncService` |
| Vault host (browser / Electron / Capacitor) | `VAULT_ENGINE_TOKEN` → `BrowserVaultEngine` / `ElectronVaultEngine` / `CapacitorVaultEngine` |
| Shared CSS shell (auth/forms) | `shared/styles/auth-shell.css`, tokens in `styles.css` |
| App chrome / content-area bounds | `--app-chrome-height`, `[data-app-content]`, `shared/ui/layout/content-area.ts` |

## Commits

Ask where the user is before committing. First line: `<place> <goal>` (Hideaway is a place-stamp, not a magic title and not assumed).

Body only when the goal needs grains above the diff. Prefer verb-led, natural bullets. Signpost with **one fixed name** per surface (class, selector, owner)—do not invent aliases for the same thing. Prefer a short domain phrase over listing every new symbol when that domain owns them. When the same commit includes a preliminary that enables the goal, list that bullet first. Track files (or their owners) nested under the domain change. Header-only when the diff is one file and obvious. Do not restate the header, the product story, or work that is not in the diff.

Fold same-story follow-ups into the unpushed commit. Leave unrelated fixes as their own commit. Do not rewrite anything already on the remote.

Only commit when the user asks.

## Comments

Comments record durable why that the code does not show. Put session teaching, warning names, and “not X” rebuttals in the chat. Do not narrate a choice the identifiers already name, or give the same UI thing a second nickname beside its class/selector.

```javascript
// BAD — conversation residue
// Electron's CSP warning is "no policy at all", not "you should load nothing".

// BAD — play-by-play the next reader gets from the bindings
// Top: whole sidebar. Bottom: lower library row when present.

// GOOD — why these two tokens exist
// 'unsafe-inline' styles: Angular/Material. wasm-unsafe-eval: sql.js (browser) / concentration worker.
```

## Tests

Specs are welcome. The Vitest DOM harness (`jsdom` / `happy-dom`) is a **known gap**—see `.cursor/FOLLOWUPS.md` when that file is present. Do not thrash `ng test`, silently add a DOM package, or treat a missing harness as a product blocker. Prefer `ng build` to verify compile until the user asks to land the harness.

## Refactors

Propose preliminary or structural cleanups that would enable the task; wait for assent before expanding into them. Do not take a blank check to retokenize the shell, reshape hit targets, etc. mid-feature.

## Session scope

Treat community sync, art download/Capacitor filesystem, and similar as **in or out of scope only when the user says so** for that session—do not assume they are permanent non-goals.

When present, read `.cursor/FOLLOWUPS.md` for intentional deferrals and tooling debt (local file; may not be in git).
